Q13-> What is the difference between session storage and local storage?

Ans-> 1. Local Storage (localStorage)
Lifespan (Duration): localStorage me save kiya gaya data hamesha ke liye rehta hai. Yeh tab tak delete nahi hota jab tak aap khud code likh kar (localStorage.removeItem()) ya browser ki settings se cache/data clear na karein.

Browser Closed: Agar aapne browser band kar diya, apna computer restart kar diya, ya kuch dino baad bhi website khole, tab bhi data wahi ka wahi milega.

Real-life example: Website ki Dark Mode / Light Mode theme preference ya user ki language setting, jise bar-bar set na karna pade.

2. Session Storage (sessionStorage)
Lifespan (Duration): sessionStorage me data sirf tab ki session-life tak rehta hai. Jaise hi aap woh specific browser tab ya window band karte hain, data apne aap delete ho jata hai.

Tab-Specific: Agar aap ek hi website ko do alag-alag tabs me kholte hain, toh dono tabs ka sessionStorage bilkul alag hoga (ek tab ka data dusre tab me share nahi hota).

Real-life example: E-commerce website par jab aap multi-step checkout form bhar rahe hote hain, toh temporary form data tab tak rakha jata hai jab tak aap order place na kardein ya tab close na kardein.

Q14-> Difference between pop and shift method.

1. pop() Method (End se remove karna)
Kaam: Yeh array ke sabse aakhri (last) element ko remove karta hai.
Performance (Time Complexity) -> Fast (O(1)) – Kyunki baaki elements ko touch nahi karna padta.

2. shift() Method (Start se remove karna)
Kaam: Yeh array ke sabse pehle (first) element ko remove karta hai.
Performance (Time Complexity) -> Slower (O(N)) – Kyunki pehla element hatane ke baad baaki sabhi elements ki position index re-adjust karni padti hai.

Q15-> Difference between slice and splice method ?

Ans-> In dono ke beech ka sabse bada aur main fark yeh hai ki slice original array ko change nahi karta (non-mutating), jabki splice original array ko modify/change kar deta hai (mutating).

1. slice() Method (Katta nahi hai, bas copy banata hai)
Kaam: Yeh original array me se ek specific portion (tukda) nikal kar ek naya array return karta hai.

Original Array: Isse original array par koi asar nahi padta (wo safe rehta hai).

let numbers = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50];

// Index 1 se lekar index 4 se pehle tak ka slice lo
let slicedArr = numbers.slice(1, 4); 

console.log(slicedArr);  // Output: [20, 30, 40]
console.log(numbers);    // Output: [10, 20, 30, 40, 50] (Original array safe hai!)

2. splice() Method (Original array me tod-फोड़ karta hai)
Kaam: Yeh original array me se elements ko delete karne, replace karne, ya naye elements add karne ke kaam aata hai.

Original Array: Yeh original array ko modify kar deta hai.

Syntax: array.splice(startIndex, deleteCount, item1, item2, ...)

startIndex: Kahan se shuru karna hai.

deleteCount: Kitne elements hatane hain.

item1, item2: Agar koi naye elements add karne hon toh.

let fruits = ["apple", "banana", "mango", "orange"];

// Index 1 se shuru karo, 2 elements delete kar do ("banana" aur "mango")
let removed = fruits.splice(1, 2);

console.log(removed); // Output: ["banana", "mango"] (Jo delete hue wo return honge)
console.log(fruits);  // Output: ["apple", "orange"] (Original array change ho gaya!)

Q16-> What are timers in JavaScript and what is their purpose?

Ans-> JavaScript me Timers kuch aisi built-in functions (ya APIs) hoti hain jo aapko yeh control dene me madad karti hain ki kisi code ko kab execute karna hai—kuch time baad ya ek fix interval par.

Kyunki JavaScript by default ek single-threaded language hai (yaani ek waqt me ek hi kaam kar sakti hai), toh timers ki madad se hum asynchronous tasks aur delayed operations ko bina main thread ko block kiye run kar sakte hain.

setTimeout(callback, delay):
Yeh diye gaye delay ke baad function ko sirf ek baar chalata hai. Isko rokne ke liye clearTimeout() use hota hai.

setInterval(callback, delay):
Yeh har fixed interval par function ko baar-baar chalata rehta hai. Isko rokne ke liye clearInterval() use hota hai.

"Timers asynchronous hote hain. Jab hum setTimeout ya setInterval set karte hain, toh JavaScript ka main thread block nahi hota. Timer ka callback Web APIs / Node Timer environment me chalta hai, aur time poora hone par wo callback Callback Queue (ya Task Queue) me chala jata hai, jahan se Event Loop usko utha kar waapas Main Stack me execution ke liye lata hai."

Q17-> Types of error in JavaScript.

Ans-> 1. SyntaxError (Grammar ki Galti)

2. ReferenceError (Aisi cheez ko bulana jo hai hi nahi)
Kab aata hai: Jab aap kisi aise variable ya function ko use karne ki koshish karte hain jo declare hi nahi hua hai ya scope me nahi hai.

3. TypeError (Galat Data Type ke sath operation karna)
Kab aata hai: Jab value ka data type waisa nahi hota jaisa aap use chahte hain. Jaise kisi non-function ko function ki tarah call karna, ya null / undefined ki property access karna.

4. RangeError (Allowed Range ke bahar value dena)
Kab aata hai: Jab koi number ya value uski defined range ke andar nahi hoti.

5. URIError (URI functions ki galti)
Kab aata hai: Jab global URI functions (encodeURI() ya decodeURI()) me koi invalid character pass kiya jata hai.

Q18-> In JavaScript, how you turn an object into an array?

Ans-> const user = {
    name: "Aniket",
    age: 24,
    profession: "Developer"
};

1. Object.keys(obj) (Sirf Keys ka Array)
Kaam: Yeh object ki saari keys (properties ke naam) ko ek array me return karta hai.

Code Example:

const keysArray = Object.keys(user);
console.log(keysArray); 
// Output: ["name", "age", "profession"]

2. Object.values(obj) (Sirf Values ka Array)
Kaam: Yeh object ki saari values ko ek array me return karta hai.

Code Example:

const valuesArray = Object.values(user);
console.log(valuesArray); 
// Output: ["Aniket", 24, "Developer"]

3. Object.entries(obj) (Keys aur Values dono ka Array - Sabse zyada pucha jata hai)
Kaam: Yeh object ki har ek key-value pair ko ek chote sub-array me daal kar ek 2D array (nested array) return karta hai.

Code Example:

const entriesArray = Object.entries(user);
console.log(entriesArray); 
// Output: [ ["name", "Aniket"], ["age", 24], ["profession", "Developer"] ]

