Q20-> Difference between synchronous and asynchronous programming.?

Ans-> 1. Synchronous Programming (Blocking)
Kaam kaise karta hai: Code line by line execute hota hai. Jab tak upar wali line ka execution poora nahi hota, tab tak code aage nahi badh sakta.

Problem: Agar beech me koi aisa task aa jaye jo bohot time leta ho (jaise server se bada data lana ya heavy calculation karna), toh poora program freeze ho jata hai jab tak wo task khatam na ho.

console.log("Pehla kaam shuru");

// Maan lijiye yeh ek heavy loop hai jo 3 second tak poora system rok dega
for(let i = 0; i < 1000000000; i++) {} 

console.log("Dusra kaam shuru");
// Output line-by-line aayega aur beech me program rukega

2. Asynchronous Programming (Non-Blocking)
Kaam kaise karta hai: Code line by line rukta nahi hai. Agar koi time-lene wala task aata hai (jaise API request ya timer), toh JavaScript usko background me bhej deta hai aur aage ka code turant execute karna shuru kar deta hai. Jab background wala task poora ho jata hai, tab uska result (callback) run hota hai.

Fayda: Isse UI freeze nahi hoti aur app fast aur smooth chalta hai.

console.log("Pehla kaam shuru");

// Yeh background me 2 second ke liye chalega, tab tak aage ka code chal jayega
setTimeout(() => {
    console.log("Background wala kaam poora ho gaya!");
}, 2000);

console.log("Dusra kaam shuru");

// Output dekhiye:
// 1. Pehla kaam shuru
// 2. Dusra kaam shuru (Ruka nahi, turant chal gaya!)
// 3. Background wala kaam poora ho gaya! (2 second baad)

"JavaScript by default ek single-threaded synchronous language hai. Lekin browser ya Node.js ke environment (Web APIs aur Event Loop) ki wajah se hum JavaScript me asynchronous programming (jaise Promises, async/await, aur setTimeout) kar pate hain, taaki heavy tasks main thread ko block na karein."

Q21->   Difference between promises and async await, which one is better?

Ans-> 1. Promises (.then() aur .catch())
Promises ko ES6 me introduce kiya gaya tha taaki callback hell (Pyramid of Doom) se bacha ja sake. Isme hum asynchronous operations ko handle karne ke liye .then() chaining ka use karte hain.

Dikkat: Jab bohot saari chains ban jaati hain (.then().then().then()), toh code ko padhna aur error handle karna thoda mushkil ho jata hai.

2. Async / Await (try...catch)
Yeh ES8 me aaya tha. Isne asynchronous code ko likhne aur samajhne ka tareeka hi badal diya. Yeh bilkul synchronous code jaisa lagta hai.

Fayda: Yeh clean, readable, aur maintain karne me bohot aasaan hota hai. Isme hum standard try...catch block use kar sakte hain jo errors ko handle karna bohot simple bana deta hai.

"Technically, async/await better mana jata hai modern applications me kyunki yeh code ko readable, clean aur debug karne me aasaan banata hai. Lekin under the hood, async/await ke peeche Promises hi kaam kar rahe hote hain."

Q22-> What are different events in JavaScript?

Ans-> 1. Mouse Events (Mouse se jude events)
Jab user mouse, trackpad, ya cursor ka use karta hai:

click: Jab user kisi element par click karta hai.

dblclick: Double click karne par.

mouseenter / mouseover: Jab mouse ka cursor kisi element ke upar aata hai.

mouseleave / mouseout: Jab mouse ka cursor element se bahar jata hai.

2. Keyboard Events (Keyboard se jude events)
Jab user keyboard ki keys ka use karta hai:

keydown: Jab user keyboard ki koi key dabata hai (press rakhta hai).

keyup: Jab user key ko chhodta hai (release karta hai).

3. Form / Input Events (Forms aur inputs se jude events)
Jab user form fields ke sath interact karta hai:

submit: Jab koi form submit hota hai.

input: Jab user input field me kuch bhi type karta hai (har character par trigger hota hai).

change: Jab input ki value change ho kar user field se बाहर (blur) jata hai (jaise dropdown me option select karna).

focus: Jab user kisi input box par click karta hai (focus me lata hai).

blur: Jab user input box se focus hata kar kahin aur click karta hai.

4. Window / Document Events (Browser state se jude events)
Jab poora page ya browser window kuch state change krti hai:

load: Jab poora webpage (images aur stylesheets ke sath) poori tarah load ho jata hai.

DOMContentLoaded: Jab sirf HTML document load aur parse ho jata hai (images ka wait nahi karta).

resize: Jab user browser window ka size chota ya bada karta hai.

scroll: Jab user page ko upar ya neeche scroll karta hai.